{"answer":"To leverage Sphinx's event system API for custom document transformations, you would register an event using the \code{add_event} method, connect a custom function to that event, and then emit the event at the appropriate time during the build process using the \code{emit} method. For example:

\code{sphinx.application.Sphinx.add_event(\\my_custom_event\)}
\code{sphinx.application.Sphinx.connect(\\my_custom_event\, my_custom_function)}
\code{sphinx.application.Sphinx.emit(\\my_custom_event\, *args)}

This allows you to inject custom behavior at specific points in the documentation build process."}

